sitive feasible triples exist, so its product maximum is interior. The constraint gradients are independent (otherwise \\(x=y=z\\), contradicting \\(xy+yz+zx=14\\)). Lagrange multipliers therefore give\n\\[\nyz=\\lambda+\\mu(y+z),\\quad\nxz=\\lambda+\\mu(x+z),\\quad\nxy=\\lambda+\\mu(x+y).\n\\]\nSubtracting pairs shows that if all three variables were distinct, then \\(x=y=z=\\mu\\), a contradiction. Thus two variables are equal.\n\nSet \\(x=y=a,\\ z=9-2a\\). Then\n\\[\n2a(9-2a)+a^2=14\n\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad\na=3\\pm\\frac{\\sqrt{39}}3.\n\\]\nThe plus sign makes \\(z<0\\), so the maximizing triple, up to permutation, is\n\\[\na=\\frac{9-\\sqrt{39}}3,\\qquad b=\\frac{9+2\\sqrt{39}}3.\n\\]\nAt this triple,\n\\[\nE_{\\min}\n=a+\\frac{2(a^2+b^2)}{a+b}\n=\\frac{279+9\\sqrt{39}}{18+\\sqrt{39}}\n=\\frac{1557-39\\sqrt{39}}{95}.\n\\]\n\nFinal answer: \\(\\displaystyle \\frac{1557-39\\sqrt{39}}{95}\\)."}],"phase":"final_answer","role":"assistant"}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"presence_penalty":0,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":"24h","reasoning":{"context":"all_turns","effort":"medium","mode":"standard","summary":null},"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"default","store":false,"temperature":1,"text":{"format":{"type":"text"},"verbosity":"medium"},"tool_choice":"auto","tool_usage":{"image_gen":{"input_tokens":0,"input_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_details":{"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":0},"total_tokens":0},"web_search":{"num_requests":0}},"tools":[],"top_logprobs":0,"top_p":0.98,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":176,"input_tokens_details":{"cache_write_tokens":0,"cached_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1242,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":755},"total_tokens":1418},"user":null,"metadata":{}}
